*Make it a celebration*

## Add African dance to your workshop

Want to get everyone moving? Then add an African dance session to your drumming workshop. We’ll teach simple, joyful moves, and live drumming keeps the energy high.

It’s especially popular for hens parties and birthdays. In fact, the dance session often becomes the highlight of the day!

Prefer to sit back and watch? Then see our [African drumming entertainment](/events/) for live performances instead.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /section %}

{% section tone="dark" %}
## What happens in a workshop

1. **Warm up:** First, fun rhythm games and movement help everyone relax.
2. **Call and response:** Next, call-and-response patterns get the group listening and playing together.
3. **Learn a rhythm:** Then we teach a traditional West African rhythm on the [djembe](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Djembe), one part at a time.
4. **Play as one:** Finally, the whole group plays together as one big ensemble.
{% /section %}

{% section tone="grey" %}
*Feel-good benefits*

## Why groups love drumming together

African drumming is more than music. It’s also a simple way to connect, unwind and have fun.

- **Physical activity:** Drumming gets your arms, shoulders and whole body moving.
- **Wellbeing:** Playing in rhythm with others lifts your mood and eases stress.
- **Coordination:** Using both hands at once also gives your brain a workout.
- **Self-expression:** Everyone adds their own voice, so creativity flows naturally.
- **Connection:** Above all, drumming builds a sense of belonging without needing words.
{% /section %}

