## African drumming workshops FAQs

{% faq %}
{% question title="Do we need any drumming experience?" %}
Not at all. Our African drumming workshops are designed for complete beginners, so everyone can join in from the very first beat.
{% /question %}

{% question title="How many people can take part?" %}
There’s no maximum group size. So whether it’s a small birthday gathering or a festival crowd, we’ll shape the workshop to suit your numbers.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Do you bring the drums?" %}
Yes. We bring West African drums and percussion for every participant, so there are no drum-hire fees.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Can we add African dance?" %}
Yes. We can add a fun African dance session, either on its own or after the drumming. It’s especially popular for hens parties.
{% /question %}

{% question title="Are workshops suitable for kids?" %}
Yes. Our workshops suit all ages, so families, library holiday programs and kids’ parties are all welcome. For school groups, see our [school incursions](/school-incursions/).
{% /question %}

{% question title="Where do you run workshops?" %}
We’re based on the Sunshine Coast and travel across South East Queensland with no travel fees. In addition, our artists can run workshops Australia-wide.
{% /question %}
{% /faq %}
{% /section %}

